  - void seek(std::int64_t ms) noexcept;
  - void update_to_now() noexcept;
  - int set_volume(int v) noexcept;
  - int volume() const noexcept;
  - void mute(bool m) noexcept;
  - bool muted() const noexcept;
  - int effective_volume() const noexcept;
  private:
  - const Time::IClock& clock_;
  - PlaybackState state_;
  - const Media::MediaMetadata* current_media_;
  - std::int64_t position_ms_;
  - std::int64_t last_tick_ms_;
  - int volume_;
  - bool muted_;
}
Contract:
- Header must directly contain #include <cstdint> and include Time/IClock.h, Media/MediaMetadata.h, and Player/PlaybackState.h.
- state_ initially Stopped; position_ms_ initially 0; current_media_ initially nullptr; last_tick_ms_ initialized from clock_.now_ms(). volume_ default 100, muted_ default false.
- set_current_media sets pointer; resets position to 0 and sets state to Stopped; updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms(). Caller owns lifetime of media; pointer may be nullptr to clear.
- current_media returns the pointer (may be nullptr).
- state returns current playback state.
- position_ms returns current position in ms; always in [0, duration]. If no media, duration is 0 and position is 0.
- duration_ms returns media duration or 0 if no media.
- play returns true if state becomes Playing (when media is set and either Stopped or Paused); returns false if no media; if already Playing, leaves state and returns true; updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms() when entering Playing.
- pause sets state to Paused if it was Playing; no-op otherwise.
- stop sets state to Stopped and position to 0; updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms().
- seek clamps ms to [0, duration]; sets position; if state is Playing and position becomes >= duration, clamps to duration and sets state to Paused (end-of-media); updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms() when state is Playing; otherwise leaves last_tick_ms_ as-is.
- update_to_now when state is Playing and media set: calculates delta = clock_.now_ms() - last_tick_ms_ (if delta <= 0, only updates last_tick_ms_); adds delta to position, clamps to duration; when clamped at end, sets state to Paused; always sets last_tick_ms_ to current clock_.now_ms(). When not Playing or no media, does nothing but may refresh last_tick_ms_ only when transitioning to Playing elsewhere.
- set_volume clamps v to [0, 100], stores, and returns the clamped value.
- volume returns the stored unclamped volume value (clamped in setter).
- mute sets muted_ flag; muted returns flag.
- effective_volume returns 0 if muted, otherwise volume().
- All methods marked noexcept in signature must not throw. All std::int64_t types are spelled exactly and headers include <cstdint> directly.

